WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.268
-President Biden signed his

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:05.538
$1.9 trillion COVID relief
bill into law today,

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.806
exactly one year after the
World Health Organization

00:00:07.806 --> 00:00:09.943
declared the coronavirus
a pandemic

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:11.711
and the country started
to shut down

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.214
and Republicans tried
to both lie about the bill

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.749
and claim credit
for the bill at the same time.

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:18.951
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:23.022
♪♪

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:24.924
Everyone's been reflecting
on the fact

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.292
that it's been
exactly one year

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.494
since the start of the pandemic
and the shutdowns

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:29.962
and, while most normal
human beings

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:33.099
have looked back solemnly
at the staggering death toll

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.334
and all the suffering,
the pain, and misery caused

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:38.471
by the economic crash,
"Fox &amp; Friends" is wondering,

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:41.574
"What if we just like
didn't do anything?"

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:45.111
You wonder where we
would've been a year ago,

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.313 line:0%
had they said, "Okay,
these are the things

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.681 line:0%
to protect yourselves,"

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.883 line:0%
but they had not closed down
the whole planet

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:53.519 line:0%
and then just given
people the choice.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:54.987 line:0%
Where would we be
one year later?

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:59.459 line:0%
Because today marks the one-year
anniversary of the pandemic.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.460 line:0%
-I know. Can you imagine where
our economy would be today,

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.429 line:0%
where our healthcare sector
would be today?

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.365 line:0%
Human beings are capable
of good decisions,

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.233 line:0%
if you provide them
with the right information.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:10.369 line:0%
It's a thought experiment,
unfortunately, Steve,

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:12.571 line:0%
we don't get to do in reverse.

00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:13.873
-I don't know, guys.
Seems like

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.708
the thought experiment
falls apart

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.143
when you talk
about providing people

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.845
with the right information,
since you work for a network

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:21.781
that might as well be called...

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.783
Let's not forget
last year's hits, like,

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.452
"It's basically the flu,"
"Masks don't work,"

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:28.788
or the doctor who said
hydroxychloroquine is the answer

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.623
is the same doctor
who also believes

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.859
demons have sex with men
to collect their sperm.

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:35.228
Do you know how hard
comedy writing is

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.897
when the real thing
is demon sperm?

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.599
You can't heighten it.
Here, I'll prove it.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:42.267
Trump's touting a doctor
who believes in demon sperm.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:44.570
What's next, demon sperm?

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.372
See?
There's nowhere else to go.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.474
Sure, I guess
I could say unicorn [bleep],

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:51.410
but they're just going to beep
[bleep]

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.213
I can't believe the question
these guys are asking,

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:56.616
after a year
and half a million deaths, is,

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.150
"What if, instead
of helping people,

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.053
we just like did nothing?"

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.788
You sociopaths.
Do you guys not understand

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.723
like the germ theory
of disease?

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:06.793
[ Dully ]
Microorganisms spread
from one person to another,

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.327
so, in order
to stop the disease,

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:09.795
you have to keep people apart.

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:11.130
I can't believe I have
to explain this to you

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.766
like I'm some
19th-century biologist.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:14.800
"You don't understand.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.602
Diseases are caused
by microbes."

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.471
Okay, Louis Pasteur.
Come on, guys.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.940
Let's go drink from the fountain
outside the asylum.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.744
I can't believe it's been a year
since everything shut down.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:27.379
And, by that,
I mean it's only been a year.

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:28.747
I feel like,
these last 12 months,

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:30.449
we've all aged
at president speed.

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:32.385
Remember how Obama went in

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.787
looking like a cast member
on "My So-Called Life"

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.088
and came out looking like

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.390
he'd just seen
Mitch McConnell's ghost?

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.525
That's all of us now.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.527
In fact, I feel like
Obama's the only one

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.662
who's somehow gotten younger
in the last year.

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:44.897
He's hanging out
on the vineyard,

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.866
doing podcasts,
like a 20-year- old stand-up.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.835
[ As Obama ]
Bruce, I, uh...

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.204
got a sweet new audio setup.

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.472
Just bought a Yeti
and a pop filter.

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:54.807
But it's true,
it's been exactly one year

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.544
since that surreal cascade
of events led

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:59.979
to the shutdown of the country,
from the NBA shutting down

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.681
to Tom Hanks getting COVID

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.616
and then, of course,
as we all solemnly remember,

00:03:04.616 --> 00:03:05.985
the late night shows.

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.320
One year ago,
I was here in my studio alone,

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.656
after sending our staff home
and canceling our show,

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.158
doing "A Closer Look"
for YouTube.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:14.961
And now, a year later,
I'm here in my studio alone,

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.929
doing "A Closer Look" for Wally.

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.564
I hope you enjoy them, Wally.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.767
-I mean, I wish they could be
a little shorter.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:21.801
-Not now, Wally.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.069
-It's really heavy to hold!

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.437
-Not now!

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.971
I remember that day
like it was yesterday.

00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:27.840
Everything was shutting down,
people were scared,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.242
grocery stores were ransacked,

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:31.310
so I got up on a chair
in the office

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.613
and gave an inspirational speech
where I said to my staff, "Gang,

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:36.548
I know you're terrified,
but this is our moment.

00:03:36.548 --> 00:03:37.850
People are counting on us.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.118
So let's get out there

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.986
and put on the best
goddamn show of our lives."

00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:42.855
And then I looked down
and the room was empty,

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.158
except for a tumbleweed
that rolled past,

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.927
stole a bottle of Purell
off my desk, and then left.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:52.231
[ Wind blowing ]

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:53.866
And it was even worse than that
because I was standing

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.702
on top of my chair
and the crew guy

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.770
who helps me down from chairs
had left.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.906
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:02.875
I don't know how to do it.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.144
I used to.

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.912
Anyway, the point is
it's worth stepping back,

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:08.681
reflecting on everything
the country's been through

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.383
over the last year --
all the pain, the suffering,

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.651
the joblessness,
rising poverty, food scarcity,

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:14.520
so much of it needless,
thanks, in large part,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.256
to the sociopathic incompetence
of an administration

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:19.559
and political party
that simply did not care

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.827
that a deadly virus was
rampaging through the country

00:04:21.827 --> 00:04:23.162
and often
did everything it could

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.230
to help spread the disease.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.965
It's also been one year

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:28.201
since we all trapped ourselves
inside our homes

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.403
with stockpiles of gin
and red wine,

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.304
watching "Tiger King"
and "Love Is Blind"

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:34.640
while clinging to our last
shreds of toilet paper,

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.243
like a plank floating
in the water after a shipwreck.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.311
Remember that?

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:40.279
When there was a deadly,
mysterious virus

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:42.782
rampaging through the country
and, instead of face masks,

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.751
everyone thought the one thing
they'd need was toilet paper?

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:47.886
I have so much residual anxiety
from that

00:04:47.886 --> 00:04:49.822
that, when I see a guy
walking down the street

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.991
with a 12-pack of Charmin
from the grocery store,

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.859
I still can't help
but think to myself,

00:04:53.859 --> 00:04:55.862
"[Bleep] you!

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.030
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.599
You better have 12 [bleep],
buddy."

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:02.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:03.969
Also, remember "Love Is Blind"?

00:05:03.969 --> 00:05:06.072
I know it was a year ago,
but we still

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:08.707
have to talk about Jessica.

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:11.877
Mostly, in regards to how she
was showing us our own futures.

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:14.146
Everyone thought it was insane
when she gave wine to her dog,

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:16.382
but then quarantine happened
and we all ended up doing

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.517
much, much weirder things
to pass the time.

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:20.586
I, for example, developed
a close personal relationship

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.355
with a sea captain painting,
so, Jessica,

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:24.890
I am very sorry for judging you.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.326
It's also been exactly one year
since our last president

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:29.662
delivered a bizarre
prime time address

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.931
where he struggled to read
off the teleprompter,

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:33.999
got a bunch
of his own policies wrong,

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:37.503
and then did this after he
thought the feed had cut out.

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.204
-We will heal the sick,

00:05:39.204 --> 00:05:42.608
care for those in need,
help our fellow citizens,

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:44.344
and emerge from this challenge

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:47.914
stronger and more unified
than ever before.

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:51.049
God bless you
and God bless America.

00:05:51.049 --> 00:05:52.285
Thank you.

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:04.230
-Thank you.
-We're clear.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.332
-Okay.

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.000
Okay. [ Sigh ]

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.702
[ Laughter ]
Remember that?

00:06:10.702 --> 00:06:13.272
When the president reacted
to his own speech

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:15.641
on a national crisis
like you just told him

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.843
you were getting back together
with your ex.

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:20.213
[ As Trump ]
She stole your car to go
have sex with your brother, but,

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.848
ah, okay!

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:24.083
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:26.085
Although, my favorite part
of that speech was actually

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:28.721
the bit C-SPAN cut
before it started,

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:31.090
when Trump accidentally
got a pen mark on his suit

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.092
and freaked out.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.661
-You have [indistinct].
-A what?

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:39.031
Oh, [bleep]

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:41.133
Uh-oh.
I got a pen mark.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.736
Anybody have any white?
Do you have any white stuff?

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.270
-That is definitely not

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.206
what you want to see
during a national emergency --

00:06:47.206 --> 00:06:50.042
tune in to C-SPAN early
and see the president saying --

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:52.178
[ As Trump ]
Uh-oh. [Bleep]

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:53.179
Oh no!

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:54.180
"What is it, Mr. President,

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.214
more bad news on the virus?"

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:56.382
No, way worse, guys.

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:59.151
I got a big old ketchup stain
on my shirt.

00:06:59.151 --> 00:07:01.620
You shouldn't have let me
have the Sloppy Joe

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:02.621
right before we went on.

00:07:02.621 --> 00:07:05.658
Does anyone have
a Tide to Go stick?

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:07.460
Tide to Go stick? Mel?!

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:08.761
[ Laughter ]

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.262
Mel?!

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:13.232
Do you have
the Tide to Go stick?

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.900
What?
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.869
Say it louder, Mel.

00:07:17.869 --> 00:07:19.004
I should Tide to [bleep]?

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:20.206
Mel!

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:21.641
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:23.542
Bring down the white stuff!

00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:25.444
No, not cocaine!
Mayonnaise!

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:28.347
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.381
You know, it's such a relief

00:07:29.381 --> 00:07:30.783
to have a competent
administration

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.584
that actually cares
about governing

00:07:32.584 --> 00:07:35.221
and a party that just passed
a massive stimulus bill

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:37.489
that will deliver urgent relief
to millions of people,

00:07:37.489 --> 00:07:38.958
as opposed to, you know,

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:41.059
a racist, authoritarian,
criminal sociopath

00:07:41.059 --> 00:07:42.428
who tried
to overthrow democracy.

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:45.231
But I will still
occasionally reminisce

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:46.899
about how deeply weird he was.

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:48.734
If Trump wants to run again,
we should just create

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.970
a second position,
separate from president,

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:53.339
and call it White House Weirdo
or something.

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:55.007
Let him hug all the flags
he wants

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:57.076
and shake Macron's hand
for an hour,

00:07:57.076 --> 00:07:58.710
while Biden does all
the actual governing.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:00.646
And let's not forget, a lot
has changed in the last year

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:03.216
for Trump, too, and not just
because of the pandemic.

00:08:03.216 --> 00:08:06.351
Now that he's lost the legal
protections of the presidency,

00:08:06.351 --> 00:08:08.220
he's under increasing
criminal scrutiny.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.755
The Wall Street Journal
obtained the audio

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:11.990
of yet another phone call
in which Trump pressured

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:14.526
a Georgia election officials
to throw out valid ballots,

00:08:14.526 --> 00:08:17.295
which comes
as the Fulton County D.A.

00:08:17.295 --> 00:08:20.132
investigates Trump's bid
to steal the state's votes

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:22.768
and his former fixer
Michael Cohen,

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:24.770
who already went to jail
for a hush money scheme

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.772
directed by Trump,
is apparently cooperating

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:28.707
with the Manhattan
District Attorney's Office

00:08:28.707 --> 00:08:31.944
in its investigation of Trump's
business dealings and taxes.

00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:33.979 line:0%
-CNN has learned
that Michael Cohen,

00:08:33.979 --> 00:08:35.814 line:0%
former Trump lawyer and fixer,

00:08:35.814 --> 00:08:37.550 line:0%
met with prosecutors from the

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.752 line:0%
Manhattan
District Attorney's Office

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:42.688 line:0%
for a seventh time,
as their investigation

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:45.157 line:0%
of the former president
continues.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:46.692
-Seven interviews.
My God, they're going to have

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:49.528
to publish the indictment
as a multipart series,

00:08:49.528 --> 00:08:50.562
like "Game of Thrones."

00:08:50.562 --> 00:08:52.231
I'm no lawyer,
but, generally speaking,

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:54.733
it's not good when the
prosecutor investigating you

00:08:54.733 --> 00:08:56.735
does more interviews
with your personal fixer

00:08:56.735 --> 00:08:58.971
than there are episodes
in an HBO miniseries.

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:01.640
When Trump heard about the
seven interviews with Cohen,

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.709
he was probably as shocked
as Nicole Kidman was

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:05.377
when she found out
her charming British husband

00:09:05.377 --> 00:09:07.679
with a mysterious past,
who's estranged from his family,

00:09:07.679 --> 00:09:10.382
and conspicuously left his phone
at home during a trip

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:11.984
that he was purposely
vague about

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:13.552
might have killed someone.

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:15.588
When Trump got the call
about Cohen's seven interviews,

00:09:15.588 --> 00:09:16.589
he probably was like --

00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:18.490
-Oh, [bleep]

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:21.326
-But Trump's bizarre
halfhearted speech one year ago

00:09:21.326 --> 00:09:23.996
is a stunning contrast with the
seriousness and gravitas

00:09:23.996 --> 00:09:26.332
of the speech President Biden
delivered tonight,

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:27.766
exactly one year later,

00:09:27.766 --> 00:09:29.368
to mark the pain
the country's endured,

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:31.937
while also offering hope
for the future.

00:09:31.937 --> 00:09:34.173
Vaccinations are ramping up,
cases are headed down,

00:09:34.173 --> 00:09:36.075
and, today, Biden signed a bill
that will inject

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:38.144
$1.9 trillion into the economy

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:40.446
to help struggling Americans
who need and deserve it.

00:09:40.446 --> 00:09:41.847
The bill's enormously popular.

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:44.883
75% of Americans
and 59% of Republicans

00:09:44.883 --> 00:09:46.785
approve of that.
Do you know how hard it is

00:09:46.785 --> 00:09:48.988
