00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:32.598
For today.

00:10:32.598 --> 00:10:33.699
[ Laughter ]
Anyway.

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.500
Point is, the bill
is massively popular

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.102
with voters in both parties
and, yet,

00:10:37.102 --> 00:10:40.138
Republicans have derided it
as a so-called partisan bill

00:10:40.138 --> 00:10:43.041
and gone so far as to pretend
that it doesn't even

00:10:43.041 --> 00:10:45.945
do that much about COVID,
which is a total lie.

00:10:45.945 --> 00:10:47.012
-I'm extremely disappointed

00:10:47.012 --> 00:10:48.380
in Nancy Pelosi
and Chuck Schumer.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.249
This is a very partisan bill.

00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:52.384
-There was no reason for them
to jam through

00:10:52.384 --> 00:10:55.287 line:0%
this $1.9 trillion bill.

00:10:55.287 --> 00:10:57.056
-I think we might have
a new name

00:10:57.056 --> 00:10:58.624
for this package
that's come over.

00:10:58.624 --> 00:11:05.864
It's the Porky Partisan, uh,
Pricy...Pet Project...Package.

00:11:05.864 --> 00:11:07.265
-It's just unbelievable.

00:11:07.265 --> 00:11:09.969 line:0%
This thing is just
so corrupt, so costly,

00:11:09.969 --> 00:11:11.670 line:0%
and you look at it,
it's just so liberal.

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:13.639 line:0%
-$1.9 trillion of relief

00:11:13.639 --> 00:11:16.341 line:0%
that mostly has nothing
to do with COVID.

00:11:16.341 --> 00:11:17.743 line:0%
-President Biden says it's

00:11:17.743 --> 00:11:20.345 line:0%
a coronavirus bill

00:11:20.345 --> 00:11:24.149 line:0%
and my response is,
"Right, you know,

00:11:24.149 --> 00:11:25.984 line:0%
and the stripper
really likes you."

00:11:25.984 --> 00:11:28.020
-What?
What are you talking about?

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.489
It says a lot about Kennedy
that he thinks that's an analogy

00:11:30.489 --> 00:11:31.991
that makes the most sense
to people.

00:11:31.991 --> 00:11:33.592
[ As Kennedy ]
We've all been there, Brian.

00:11:33.592 --> 00:11:36.128
You're at the club
and you strike up a conversation

00:11:36.128 --> 00:11:37.296
with one of the dancers --

00:11:37.296 --> 00:11:39.665
Misty's my favorite --
and you make it feel

00:11:39.665 --> 00:11:41.032
like you're having
a real connection.

00:11:41.032 --> 00:11:42.334
Next thing you know,
you go in for a hug

00:11:42.334 --> 00:11:44.804
and the bouncer's throwing you
out on the sidewalk,

00:11:44.804 --> 00:11:46.772
telling you you're banned
from The Diamond Donkey,

00:11:46.772 --> 00:11:49.608
which is bad news because they
got the best shrimp in town.

00:11:49.608 --> 00:11:50.976
And that's
what this COVID bill is.

00:11:50.976 --> 00:11:52.344
It just the strip club shrimp.

00:11:52.344 --> 00:11:54.646
You can't have it anymore.

00:11:54.646 --> 00:11:56.248
It's all COVID money.

00:11:56.248 --> 00:11:58.250
The $1,400 checks,
that's COVID money.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.384
The money to reopen schools,

00:11:59.384 --> 00:12:01.453
fund state and local governments
to pay pensions,

00:12:01.453 --> 00:12:03.522
to keep services running
and people employed,

00:12:03.522 --> 00:12:04.756
that's COVID money, too.

00:12:04.756 --> 00:12:05.890
Bot to mention the money

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:07.559
for vaccinations
and public health.

00:12:07.559 --> 00:12:10.629
But Kennedy continued
with his deranged analogy.

00:12:10.629 --> 00:12:12.698
-It's just chock full
of spending porn.

00:12:12.698 --> 00:12:15.867 line:0%
And, if you add up all
the coronavirus spending

00:12:15.867 --> 00:12:19.338 line:0%
and then, all the spending porn,
there's no comparison

00:12:19.338 --> 00:12:22.074 line:0%
and, to me,

00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:28.747 line:0%
using a coronavirus bill
to effectuate spending porn

00:12:28.747 --> 00:12:31.884 line:0%
is like looting
after a natural disaster.

00:12:31.884 --> 00:12:33.786
-Jesus, dude,
I don't love "Fox &amp; Friends,"

00:12:33.786 --> 00:12:35.720
but it's a morning show.
You can't come out

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:37.889
firing "strippers"
and "porn" everywhere.

00:12:37.889 --> 00:12:39.391
I mean, save something
for Hannity.

00:12:39.391 --> 00:12:40.759
What's left for him?

00:12:40.759 --> 00:12:43.229
[ As Kennedy ] I want to talk
about unicorn [bleep]

00:12:43.229 --> 00:12:45.030
[ Laughter ]

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.298
You're a weird man.

00:12:46.298 --> 00:12:47.465
I can't follow a word
you're saying.

00:12:47.465 --> 00:12:48.934
Are you trying to sound
like Boomhauer?

00:12:48.934 --> 00:12:51.337
Because that interview
would actually make more sense.

00:12:51.337 --> 00:12:53.872 line:0%
-Are you celebrating the
greatest progressive bill

00:12:53.872 --> 00:12:55.207 line:0%
in the history of our country?

00:12:55.207 --> 00:12:57.843 line:0%
-We go --
[ Continues indistinctly ]

00:12:57.843 --> 00:12:59.712 line:0%
man, a little --
with a little squirt gun.

00:12:59.712 --> 00:13:02.113
-But I have to say, some of the
most galling behavior came

00:13:02.113 --> 00:13:03.482
from Republicans
who actually tried

00:13:03.482 --> 00:13:05.217
to take credit
for elements of the bill,

00:13:05.217 --> 00:13:06.685
while also voting against it.

00:13:06.685 --> 00:13:09.488
-Republican Senator Roger Wicker
of Mississippi tweeted today,

00:13:09.488 --> 00:13:15.728
after the bill passed the House,
he tweeted...

00:13:24.603 --> 00:13:26.371 line:0%
Sounds like he's all for it

00:13:26.371 --> 00:13:29.574 line:0%
-Sure does.
-and was part of passing it.

00:13:29.574 --> 00:13:31.477 line:0%
He actually voted
against the bill,

00:13:31.477 --> 00:13:33.645 line:0%
as did every single Republican
in the Congress.

00:13:33.645 --> 00:13:35.647
-You voted against it.
If you'd gotten your way,

00:13:35.647 --> 00:13:37.682
