a dime of that money.

00:13:37.682 --> 00:13:39.584
You can't just turn around
and claim credit for it.

00:13:39.584 --> 00:13:42.320
I know these guys are shameless,
but I'm still shocked.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:43.688
They're the kind of guys
who would run out

00:13:43.688 --> 00:13:45.557
and try to lift Tom Brady
on their shoulders

00:13:45.557 --> 00:13:46.991
while wearing Chiefs jerseys.

00:13:46.991 --> 00:13:48.226
We're like a week away

00:13:48.226 --> 00:13:49.862
from them going door to door,
scribbling...

00:13:51.296 --> 00:13:53.632
...in the memo line
of everyone's stimulus check.

00:13:53.632 --> 00:13:56.367
It has been a surreal
and heartbreaking year

00:13:56.367 --> 00:13:58.737
of pain, suffering, and misery
for millions of people

00:13:58.737 --> 00:14:00.572
and, while we're
at a crossroads, right now,

00:14:00.572 --> 00:14:03.342
with a mix of caution
and competent governance,

00:14:03.342 --> 00:14:04.676
we can get to the end
of this soon,

00:14:04.676 --> 00:14:06.978
but we can't forget
the lessons of the past.

00:14:06.978 --> 00:14:09.414
One of our two
major political coalitions

00:14:09.414 --> 00:14:11.250
became unmoored from reality,

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.084
dismissed an urgent
public health threat,

00:14:13.084 --> 00:14:14.953
and presided over needless
suffering and death,

00:14:14.953 --> 00:14:16.621
all while trying
to overthrow democracy

00:14:16.621 --> 00:14:18.556
and, now,
exactly one year later,

00:14:18.556 --> 00:14:20.926
the other coalition,
whatever its faults,

00:14:20.926 --> 00:14:22.694
has delivered urgent relief
to the poor

00:14:22.694 --> 00:14:24.996
and working-class Americans
who need and deserve it.

00:14:24.996 --> 00:14:26.699
Relief that's massively popular

00:14:26.699 --> 00:14:29.134
with a majority of Americans
of all political persuasions.

00:14:29.134 --> 00:14:32.838
So, Republicans,
